Title: AROS: main menu in the window's Intuition menu
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series; aros-sdl SDL3 patch 0005-program-menu-strip
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: On AROS the commands sat in a menu bar drawn inside the window; the system menu (right mouse button on the title bar) only had SDL's own Project/Options menu.
Change: she gets a small AROS interface (she/aros_menu.h) over the aros-sdl window properties. app/ui/aros_menu_strip.cpp builds a GadTools menu from gui.xml main_menu (titles, items, one submenu level; Ctrl+letter shortcuts also as Amiga+letter), reserves the check mark column on every item and updates enabled and checked flags on IDCMP_MENUVERIFY. Structure changes (recent files, scripts list, shortcut reload) rebuild the strip at once when the menu is not in use, otherwise after it closes; a signature check in MENUVERIFY catches unreported changes. A pick from a menu shown before a rebuild is ignored. Commands are enabled and run only while the main window is in the foreground (same rule as keyboard shortcuts in app/modules/gui.cpp), checked again when the pick runs from the UI loop. The in-window menu bar is hidden once the strip is installed. SDL3Display::nativeHandle returns the Intuition window.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16: menu from the title bar, repeated opens, File > New, Amiga+N, View check marks, menu bar stays hidden; after review fixes: with the Open or Save dialog open all commands are disabled and Amiga+N does nothing; F3 (onion skin) shows its check mark on the first opening; Open Recent lists files saved with Ctrl+S without a menu pick in between
Removal: AROS-specific; upstream only together with an SDL interface for native menus.
